  "text": "That's the ten traps. Now, four questions, one answer each. Variance is the average squared distance from the mean. Standard deviation is its square root, back in the data's own units. Ten to fifty gives two fifty and fifteen point eight one. Pandas divides by n minus one. The mode is the most common value, and the center that works for categories: the most common ticket is billing. Two modes are a reason to split the data. A normal distribution is a symmetric bell, set by its mean and standard deviation. Sixty-eight percent falls within one standard deviation, ninety-five within two, ninety-nine point seven within three. And the population is everyone you care about. A sample is the part you measured, and its mean is only an estimate. Three samples of fifty give fifty-two point one, fifty-one point eight and fifty-one point one. The population's mean is fifty point two. Back to SQL, for the questions that turn a good screen into a great one: rankings, running totals, and the latest row per customer. Next: advanced SQL.",
